// 79 — a panic guard leaves what follows it unnested
// Exercises: one function of 200 integer divisions, 260 reads of a
//            fixed-size array at an index known only when it runs and 260
//            `u8` remainders, each behind a check that panics on a bad
//            operand.  A panic does not return, so the code after a check
//            runs beside it, not inside it: the C is no deeper for these
//            920 checks (a division has two) than for one, where clang
//            rejects brackets nested past 256, and the compile time grows
//            with the function's length.  The checks still panic: a
//            divisor of zero would.
// expect-stdout: quotients: 66666600
// expect-stdout: reads: 780
// expect-stdout: remainders: 8

import ::io;

fn id(x: int) -> int => x;

fn small(x: u8) -> u8 => x;

